                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b3cf18e5-3743-3cee-a7de-6a8ed95b4a9c",
                        "entry_id": "bd381805-25a4-3d42-a8f7-54fa19b40ee6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone or something which cans."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a506efb6-9148-47ab-9220-c284ab909cfe",
                                "sense_id": "b3cf18e5-3743-3cee-a7de-6a8ed95b4a9c",
                                "text": "One machine in which Mr. Taylor takes special pride is a salmon canner, which engulfs a whole salmon, decapitates and decaudates it, skins it, blows out its viscera, cuts it into pieces, deposits them in the can, sterilizes them […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "124349c9-52b6-3d06-afc0-9205bd79286c",
                        "entry_id": "bd381805-25a4-3d42-a8f7-54fa19b40ee6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A large pot used for processing jars when preserving food, either in a boiling water bath or by capturing steam to elevate the pressure and temperature."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3afc380c-d9a0-3f86-8f9d-3929b7c367c7",
                        "entry_id": "bd381805-25a4-3d42-a8f7-54fa19b40ee6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who lives off container deposit refunds from recycling."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6a42564-a86f-4441-9fe2-3a43eba670f4",
                                "sense_id": "3afc380c-d9a0-3f86-8f9d-3929b7c367c7",
                                "text": "Yet many canners told me that they can easily earn a daily wage of 20 or 30 dollars; each then recycles upward of 600 containers every day."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "41021666-6293-43c3-88bb-f83d5224987f",
                                "sense_id": "3afc380c-d9a0-3f86-8f9d-3929b7c367c7",
                                "text": "Among the crowds are ordinary working people shopping at the Pathmark, as well as down-and-out \"canners\" bringing their cans and bottles to the recycling station on East 124th Street."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f8d81103-e792-326b-9f3d-c4d5079ff7ae",
                        "entry_id": "bd381805-25a4-3d42-a8f7-54fa19b40ee6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An animal yielding inferior meat best suited to canning."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7211914-c066-49db-87dd-a95841959439",
                                "sense_id": "f8d81103-e792-326b-9f3d-c4d5079ff7ae",
                                "text": "Bulls and cows used for breeding, when finally sent to market, are inferior for dressed-beef production. Bulls are demanded especially for sausage and similar products. Cows are largely used as cutters and canners […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
